diff --git a/crates/sdk-core/README.md b/crates/sdk-core/README.md
index 18528a6f..29b9ce3f 100644
--- a/crates/sdk-core/README.md
+++ b/crates/sdk-core/README.md
@@ -9,3 +9,19 @@ The shared worker runtime used to build Temporal language SDKs.
 
 Its APIs are intended for SDK implementers and may change without notice. Rust application authors
 should use [`temporalio-sdk`](https://crates.io/crates/temporalio-sdk) instead.
+
+## Experimental JVM build
+
+With [`rustc_codegen_jvm`](https://github.com/IntegralPilot/rustc_codegen_jvm) installed and
+`cargo-jvm` configured to use its [`experimental2` revision
+`99ff1bd`](https://github.com/IntegralPilot/rustc_codegen_jvm/commit/99ff1bd), run:
+
+```sh
+cargo jvm build --locked -p temporalio-sdk-core --lib --no-default-features \
+  --config 'build.rustflags = ["--cfg", "getrandom_backend=\"custom\""]'
+```
+
+The JVM build uses the compiler runtime's Java `SecureRandom` implementation for system entropy.
+A JVM host must supply an RPC transport through the client service override. The command builds the
+Core library for use by a JVM bridge. Running a worker also requires that bridge to provide
+the transport and drive workflow activations.
